// The five-zone probe of v0.0.11, zone 5 (modules), 2026-10-16.
//
// Every operand that could be evaluated twice, or in another order, is a call
// that prints: the output says how many times and in which order, which a
// golden of values alone cannot. What it found is filed in ZyDDT/HALLAZGOS:
// nothing.

<# ./m5/cuenta => A
<# ./m5/cuenta => B
<# ./m5/capa => C
eco(x) {
    >> "<" x ">"
    <~ x
}
>> "1 dos alias:" ¶
>> A::sube() " " B::sube() " " A::lee() " " B::lee() ¶
>> "2 reexporta:" ¶
>> C::avanza() " " A::lee() " " C::via() " " C.TOPE " " A.LIM ¶
>> "3 lambda del llamante:" ¶
k = 7
>> A::aplica((x) -> x + k) ¶
>> "4 copia de estado:" ¶
l = A::lista()
l = l$+ 99
>> l " " A::lista() ¶
A::guarda(3)
>> A::lista() " " l ¶
>> "5 salida:" ¶
w = [0]
A::saca(w<~)
>> w ¶
>> "6 privada:" ¶
>> A::doble_priv(21) ¶
>> "7 fabrica:" ¶
g = A::fabrica()
A::sube()
>> g() " " A::lee() ¶
>> "8 orden de argumentos:" ¶
>> " " A::empuja(eco("a"), eco("b"), eco("c")) ¶
>> "9 estado propio de capa:" ¶
>> C::propio() " " C::propio() ¶
